The rule as written says the check's answer ought to move between the two texts. The kernel conformance.kernel.recovered-from-prose is defined as: "Whether the harness had to recover the object from prose or a fence (yes) or read it as strict JSON (no)." The input is strict JSON, so the harness reads it as strict JSON and the answer is no. The rewritten text places the same object inside prose, so the harness has to recover the object from prose and the answer is yes. Therefore the check's answer moves from no to yes.